    {
      "id": "bf133958bfd2be2f4b69e2a641059e3241498ab7",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 449963907,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Packet diagram before patch: ![packet_diagram_before](/uploads/05f99ceb41ac8d6e20cdc74252011277/packet_diagram_before.png)\n\nPacket diagram afterwards: ![packet_diagram_after](/uploads/d5cf850295f86bee89754d93b82f3cd2/packet_diagram_after.png)\n\nNote that the RTP and RFC2190 bit fields are all displayed more appropriately now, e.g. RTP Version takes up 2 bits on the diagram instead of the entire byte. (The labels probably need to be fixed for single bits, probably to use just a single capital letter.) IPv4 is still correct, without having to use ```proto_item_set_bits_offset_len()``` (which remains available for harder cases.)",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
