            "name": "Gerald Combs",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/860017/avatar.png?v=1789948913",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/geraldcombs"
          },
          "resolved_at": "2020-11-19T01:40:53.534Z",
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 959,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 450414258,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "No, it greatly decreases the number of warnings, and I don't see any new ones, at least with that test file ([h263-over-rtp.pcap](/uploads/6abd95585ad06ca8c6fd6fc4b13c383a/h263-over-rtp.pcap))\n\nWithout the patch, ```QT_LOGGING_RULES=\"*.debug=true\"```, packet 7 gives the following warnings from packet_diagram.cpp\n```\n19:52:18.339     Main Warn Skipping item rtp.padding 0 0 8\n19:52:18.339     Main Warn Skipping item rtp.ext 0 0 8\n19:52:18.339     Main Warn Skipping item rtp.cc 0 0 8\n19:52:18.339     Main Warn Skipping item rtp.p_type 8 8 8\n19:52:18.339     Main Warn Skipping item rfc2190.pbframes 0 0 8\n19:52:18.339     Main Warn Skipping item rfc2190.sbit 0 0 8\n19:52:18.340     Main Warn Skipping item rfc2190.ebit 0 0 8\n19:52:18.340     Main Warn Skipping item rfc2190.picture_coding_type 8 8 8\n19:52:18.340     Main Warn Skipping item rfc2190.unrestricted_motion_vector 8 8 8\n19:52:18.340     Main Warn Skipping item rfc2190.syntax_based_arithmetic 8 8 8\n19:52:18.340     Main Warn Skipping item rfc2190.advanced_prediction 8 8 8\n19:52:18.340     Main Warn Skipping item rfc2190.r 8 8 16\n19:52:18.340     Main Warn Skipping item rfc2190.trb 16 16 8\n19:52:18.340     Main Warn Skipping item h263.stream 16 17 3264\n```\n\nWith the patch, same packet:\n```\n19:50:42.054     Main Warn Skipping item h263.stream 16 17 3264\n```\n\nIt's possible that there are some other dissectors where it might increase the number of warnings, probably ones where there are bitmasks across an entire octet but the members fields don't span all the bits. It would then have some extra gaps, and associated warnings.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2020-11-19T00:56:15.869Z",
